    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0891" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg807"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>No. 394.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 4,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Porter asks whether an early date for a definite answer can be named. He
                    states that if the President is compelled to delay his action such inconvenience
                    and loss will be caused that the postponement can not be long continued.</p>
            </div>
